name: Distinguish selected scan history from the displayed observation
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR NODE_OPTIONS KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/group_runs.py prepare @TMP_TARGET @ART
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: groups
require-live-snap: 25 1 group / 1 finding | selected-history
expect: latest observations
ask: Does grouped Review make clear that the selected scan filters observation history while the displayed finding uses the current ledger?
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Observation run: latest-observation | current-observation
expect: Observed in selected runs: middle-observation
expect: Compare source revisions
ask: Can the operator distinguish the middle run that observed this finding from its displayed latest observation without an implied fixed verdict?
resize: 40x12
live-snap: narrow-history
keys: PageDown
live-snap: narrow-detail
keys: PageDown
live-snap: narrow-membership
keys: PageDown
live-snap: narrow-observation-run
expect: latest-observation
keys: PageDown
live-snap: narrow-selected-run
expect: middle-observation
keys: PageDown
live-snap: narrow-history-guidance
expect: Compare source revisions
keys: PageDown
live-snap: narrow-source-guidance
keys: PageDown
live-snap: narrow-verdict-guidance
ask: At 40x12 can the operator read the history and observation details through paging while retaining selection and usable back/open controls?
resize: 120x36
keys: Home
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 SELECTED FINDING | opened-current
keys: G
require-live-snap: 25 GROUP MEMBERS | returned-member
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/group_runs.py verify @TMP_TARGET @ART
ask: Does opening and returning preserve the selected run context and exact displayed observation, without another scan or finding decision?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME NO_COLOR=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: groups
require-live-snap: 25 1 group / 1 finding | recovered-history
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Observed in selected runs: middle-observation | recovered-member
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/group_runs.py verify @TMP_TARGET @ART
ask: Does restart preserve selected history and the latest observation in no-color output, with no provider request or inferred fix?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
